## Unused arguments required by a Protocol or framework signature

When a function must accept arguments it doesn't use (Protocol implementation, FastAPI lifespan, decorator wrapper, mock validator, etc.), suppress `ARG001` with a per-parameter `# noqa: ARG001` comment. Put each parameter on its own line.

```python
async def validator(
    *,
    raw_result: Result,
    context: Context,  # noqa: ARG001
    is_final_attempt: bool,  # noqa: ARG001
    metadata: Metadata,  # noqa: ARG001
) -> LLMGenerationResult[Result]: ...
```

**Do not** use `del context, is_final_attempt, metadata` to silence the lint. It works, but it's not the project's style — the codebase uses `# noqa: ARG001` exclusively (see `services/*/infrastructure/services/*/validators.py`, `library/library/infrastructure/cloud/base.py`, `library/library/presentation/api/app.py`).
